## Summary

Problem: The main REPL loop in repl.rs had a ~55-line inline watch-fix loop that duplicated the run_watch_after_prompt() function in watch.rs. The only difference was the inline version captured last_tool_error from fix attempts, which the shared function discarded.

Changes:

1. `src/watch.rs` — Added WatchResult struct with passed: bool and last_tool_error: Option<String>. Changed `run_watch_after_prompt to return WatchResult instead of bool`, capturing the fix outcome's last_tool_error at each attempt (previously discarded with `_fix_outcome`). Added 4 tests for the new struct.

2. `src/repl.rs` — Replaced the 55-line inline watch loop (lines 788-844) with a 10-line call to run_watch_after_prompt, using the returned WatchResult to update last_error when the watch fails.

3. `src/prompt.rs` — Trimmed re-exports to only items still used outside watch.rs (removed `build_watch_fix_prompt, run_watch_command, WatchResult, MAX_WATCH_FIX_ATTEMPTS` which were only consumed by the now-removed inline code).

Net result: -77 lines from the inline duplication, +101 lines including the richer return type, tests, and improved docs. The inline 55-line block became a clean 10-line call with identical behavior.

